-- title:
--   Fixed field of level automorphisms at q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Write $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ for the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H}(q^2M')$, $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the units of $\mathbb Z/q^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, and assume that the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the expansions $j(d\tau)$, $d\mid M'$, is contained in it (hypothesis `hle`). Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q$ containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi$. Let $H_1$ be the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ with the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$, let $K$ be the $k_0$-subfield of $k_0((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb Q$-rational function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, let $G\le \mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K)$ be the subgroup generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt` for $k_0$, $q$, $\xi$, $q$, $q^2M'$, $H_1$, $\gamma^{-1}$, $K$, $\tau$ — that is, for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\ne 0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota(\tau x)\cdot (g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge = (f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^\wedge$ as $q$-expansions, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma = \begin{pmatrix}a & b/q\\ qc & d\end{pmatrix}$. Put $K_0=K^G$. Then, with $k_0$ acting on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ consisting exactly of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $k_0$, there is a $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi:K_0\xrightarrow{\sim}F_0$ such that the coefficientwise extension of every $f\in K_0$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi(f)$, and such that for every $g$ in the $\mathbb Q$-field generated by the expansions $j(d\tau)$, $d\mid M'$, whose image in $k_0((q))$ lies in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends that element to the image of $g$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$, viewed in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`.
--
--   This is the isomorphism half of the dictionary between the fixed field of the group of level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and the subfield of $q$-expansions with coefficients in $k_0$, in the $q=3$ case with the auxiliary diamond level $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ built into $H_1$. It feeds the assembly of the full fixed-field correspondence with linked scalars, which underlies the Galois-theoretic description of the relevant modular function fields.
